Description: Let cryptsetup choose the LUKS2 encryption sector size
 KPMcore 26.08 passes "--sector-size 4096" to "cryptsetup luksFormat" for
 every LUKS2 volume (upstream commit 25d3a793, 2026-02-09). cryptsetup then
 refuses a partition whose size is not a multiple of 4096 bytes: "Device size
 is not aligned to requested sector size." Calamares 3.3.14 aligns the
 partition it creates only in its "Erase disk" path (Ubuntu's
 align-end-sector-to-4k.patch, LP: #2165428); "Replace a partition" keeps the
 old partition's exact bounds and "Install alongside" starts two sectors past
 the size slider's position, so an encrypted install in either mode fails
 while formatting the root volume.
 .
 Without the option cryptsetup selects the sector size itself
 (lib/setup.c, LUKS2 format): 4096 when the drive reports 4K physical sectors
 and the device size is a multiple of it, otherwise 512, with the log line
 "Device size is not aligned to sector size. Reverting to 512 bytes." The
 other options KPMcore sets (key size, hash, PBKDF) are unchanged.
